    "gradient_survives_the_exposure": false,
    "default_barrier_separates_from_no_barrier": false,
    "finding": "The drug field equilibrates to near uniform within the exposure durations the platform runs, and the default barrier strength is close to indistinguishable from no barrier at all. The mechanism is present in the code and quantitatively inert here. The ECM field averages a small fraction of its maximum, so the attenuation term reduces diffusivity modestly rather than blocking transport.",
    "why_it_matters": "Desmoplastic protection is the model's headline mechanism and the reason it claims to add something a ligand-based score cannot. If it does not bite, simulated growth inhibition is a restatement of the IC50 handed to it, which is what the failing positive control shows."
  },
